From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 16:39:43 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] soc: google: aoc: do not fill a ring that is already at its
 start

aoc_ring_reset_write_pointer() moves a ring's write pointer back to the
start by advancing it over the rest of the ring. When the pointer is
already at the start (wp 0, as on a ring never written), that advances
it by a whole ring: the ring then reads as full, and the first PCM write
after prepare finds no room. On gs201 the AoC does not drain such a
ring, so playback fails at once:

  ERR: inconsistent write/read pointers, avail = 0, towrite = 15360
  (audio_playback5 down ring: written 8388608, read 0)

Leave the ring alone when the write pointer is already at the start.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/soc/google/aoc/aoc_ipc_core.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/google/aoc/aoc_ipc_core.c b/drivers/soc/google/aoc/aoc_ipc_core.c
index daf3423c3..bc506513e 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/google/aoc/aoc_ipc_core.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/google/aoc/aoc_ipc_core.c
@@ -593,6 +593,14 @@ bool aoc_ring_reset_write_pointer(aoc_service *service, aoc_direction dir)
 	wp = ioread32(&r->wp);
 	bytes_remaining = sz - wp;
 
+	/*
+	 * Already at the ring start (a ring never written, or one that ended
+	 * on a wrap): nothing to skip. Advancing by a whole ring here would
+	 * mark it full of stale data, and the first write would find no room.
+	 */
+	if (wp == 0)
+		return true;
+
 	if (bytes_remaining > 0)
 		_region_advance_tx(r, bytes_remaining);
 
